If $f$ is bounded, then $sup_[a, b] abs(f) = k$ for some $k$, and every lower and upper sum obeys

$
  -k (b-a) <= L(f, cal(P)) <= U(f, cal(P)) <= k (b-a).
$

In particular $U(f, cal(P)) >= L(f, cal(P))$, so both

$
  {L(f, cal(P)): cal(P) "is a partition of" [a, b]} quad "and" quad {U(f, cal(P)): cal(P) "is a partition of" [a, b]}
$

are non-empty bounded sets.
